Subject: chunk: fsync() request-body temp files after writing on VMS

Request bodies over 64 KB are spooled to a temporary file and later read
back, through another descriptor, to forward them to a FastCGI/proxy
backend.  On OpenVMS a descriptor sees a file's end-of-file mark as it was
when that descriptor last synchronised with the file; data written through
another, still open, descriptor is beyond it until that descriptor is
flushed (same effect as patch 0007 for logs; probes/r_tmpfile.c, and
vms-mariadb DECISIONS D10).  pread() then returned 0 at offset 0 of a
65535-byte spool file, the backend write failed and the client got 503
(Phase 3: every POST/upload over 64 KB).

On VMS, fsync() the temp file after each write into it.  This only costs
on request bodies large enough to be spooled.

--- a/src/chunk.c
+++ b/src/chunk.c
@@ -1062,6 +1062,10 @@
 	      #endif
 
 		if ((size_t) written == len) {
+		  #ifdef __VMS
+			/* make the data visible to other descriptors (EOF mark) */
+			fsync(dst_c->file.fd);
+		  #endif
 			dst_c->file.length += len;
 			dest->bytes_in += len;
 			return 0;
